<<~ ahu slot=`#/b3-capstack-stages-reader-three-cold-read-2026-1`>>

! b3-capstack-stages ~ Reader-Three (Tasked Spirit), cold read, 2026-10-31
Lares (Ink-Clerk) read every line of packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts 709-1745 (main checkout, 27bc0cb6b), selfSlotShareDecision whole (self-slot-share.ts, 148L), protected-doc-guard.ts whole, and ralias's diff against 27bc0cb6b (open-node-vessel hunks, vessel-private.ts, kahu-realm.ts). Line numbers are main-checkout lines; ralias shifts them by about +45 after line 850.

Note: the source carries no "R1-R19" labels in this span (only "R3" at 1714). I name stages S0-S18 below and map them to the lift map's R-range by content.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/findings`>>

!! FINDINGS (none a live fault I could prove; three latent, one drift)

F1 LATENT, ORDER-HELD: three share-verdict inputs read OPEN while their cell holds null.
* antigenRing null: `presenterIsKapaed` answers false (federation-gate.ts:298). Stood at 1198.
* edgeShadows null: `presenterStandsAside(null)` answers false (federation-gate.ts:126). Stood at 1416 (floor: floorShadowRing wraps it).
* kahuProtected null: the guard's `ids` returns the empty map, `incomplete` reads false, `settled` resolves (849-861). So every Kahu-canon document reads UNCLASSED until the holder stands inside `systemCanon` (about 1988).
Safe today only because no wire or sibling peer can arrive before the sync gates stand (3272, inside openDaemon), the dial (2339) or the sibling channel (2669), and `systemCanon` runs earlier in composeCoreVessel (comment at 1971: "Core assembly asks before the daemon mount loads"). I verified the line order, NOT the composeCoreVessel call order, and NOT whether a floor (sovereign=null) composition still runs systemCanon. A stage-cut that moves standSyncGates, the dial or the sibling stand ahead of systemCanon opens the Kahu canon silently. Contrast ralias's vesselPrivate book, which stands at the top of the function (about 728) and so does not carry this hole. Cure shape: the ShareInputs cell answers "not stood" = withhold for these three, red-first. (Whether that tightens behavior is a ruling; see T11.)
F2 FAIL-CLOSED (checked, recorded so a cut keeps it): every other null cell reads closed. siblingGate null denies; selfSlotFedGate null becomes DenyAllGate (self-slot-share.ts:131, 146); nexusMembership null leaves a stranger; planeSeal registry empty denies; houseIslands starts as an empty Set so an unproven peer reads as WIRE (P26); an unmapped wire peer has class undefined and reaches the shelf only; guard deciders that throw or are missing withhold; ralias's `faceGrantRing` null makes the vessel-private decider answer false.
F3 DRIFT RISK (T11 relevant): the closure formula `hasWsSocket: !!wsSocket || (!houseIslands.has(peerId) && !siblings?.provenKeyOf(peerId))` (1036) and the outer gate `wsSocket && !peerIdentifierMap.has(peerId) -> false` (1027) live ONLY in the boot closure. The tests that drive selfSlotShareDecision (13 files) hand-assemble the inputs (kahu-guard-lanes.test.ts:62-67 passes `hasWsSocket: !inProcess(house, peerId)` from its own copy). The production derivation is exercised only by whole boots. A copy that drifts stays green.
F4 ORDER DEPENDENCE (fails CLOSED when broken, liveness not leak): the verdict yields one microtask (1023) so the `peer-candidate` listener registered at 907 (before `new Repo` at 997) fills peerIdentifierMap/peerClassMap/peerSessions first. Move the listener after the Repo and a same-operator peer reads class undefined and wire: shelf only, no sync. Also TDZ: `siblings`, `siblingGate`, ralias's `faceGrantRing` are `let`s declared after the guard closure that reads them; a call before their declaration throws, and the guard converts a throw to withhold.
F5 DEAD LANES: `peerContractNymMap` (876) is never `.set` anywhere (grep: reads at 1366 and 2226 only), so `realmNymOfPeer` always answers null. `walkerBoard` is never passed by the vessel (only self-slot-share.test.ts:214), and the walker arms ship SHUT (comment 3270), so the walker branches of selfSlotShareDecision (117-124) run only in tests. Old shapes burn: both are burn candidates (ruling, T11/T13).

<<~/ahu>>

