<<~ ahu slot=`#/share-verdict-walk-each-branch-open-or-closed`>>

!! Share-verdict walk (security class): each branch, open or closed
selfSlotShareDecision (self-slot-share.ts:95-143), as the closure feeds it:
# Outer gate (1027): ws socket present and no identifier -> DENY (closed). In-process or dial-adapter peer -> continues.
# presenterStandsAside(shadow) -> DENY. shadow null -> continue (OPEN while null; F1).
# Guard: `(hasWsSocket || sibling) && protectedDocs.withholds` -> DENY. classOf undefined doc -> not classed, continues (a docless ask falls to later "deny-by-default" lanes); map throw/incomplete/no decider/no peer -> withhold (closed). Ids empty while kahuProtected null (OPEN; F1).
# Sibling: also WS -> DENY; Kapae'd -> DENY; else siblingGate (null -> DENY).
# Same-operator WS: Kapae'd -> DENY; sessionFace allows -> ALLOW; else fall through to the shelf (transport grants no readership).
# WS walker/contracted special docs (never reached for walkers in production, F5); hosting docs for contracted via antigen-checked carry decision.
# Shelf: carrierShareDecision with fedGate or DenyAll (closed), membership/planeSeal closed-set blind-transit.
# In-process (not WS, proven house or, with no socket, not wire): carryContractShareDecision with empty relay ring -> allow unless Kapae'd. The only OPEN-by-design lane; it rests on `houseIslands` proof. A wrongly proven house peer reads everything. `houseIslands` fills through `markIslandArrival` in mesh (island-repo.ts:123): the proof lives in mesh, not here.
Ralias additions (committed in its wt, 589ac5d3f, not yet on the span branch): third class "vessel-private" in the SAME guard, decided by relation (sibling+gate, same-operator view of the owning face, face-join grant), owner read first; `incomplete` also reads `vesselPrivate.torn()`; `onBound` re-asks verdicts via `reverdictLater`. All branches close on missing owner/relation. I found no fail-open in the diff. One point to re-check in ralias's own read: `protectedIds` memo keys on map identity plus `priv.size`; kahu `ids()` swaps a new Map per recount (kahu-realm.ts:573 `ids: () => map`, replaced at recount), so identity change invalidates; vesselPrivate mutates its Set in place and size catches growth. Sound, but it rests on both facts staying true.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/per-candidate-reports`>>

!! Per-candidate reports

!!! T11 ShareInputs (span: shareConfig closure 1016-1067 + cell declarations 952-996 + selfSlotShareDecision whole)
# Span: open-node-vessel.ts:1016-1067 (closure) with its cells at 827, 863-872, 955-996, 1005-1087; self-slot-share.ts:1-148.
# Does: turns a (peerId, documentId) ask into a boolean on both automerge-repo hooks (`shareConfigOf`, mesh federation-gate.ts:602). The closure derives hasWsSocket/sibling/peerClass from 15 cells; selfSlotShareDecision applies the lane law.
# State: reads the cells above; writes none. Clock: none. Env: `LAR_WIRE_LOG` (990). The one yield at 1023 depends on listener order (F4).
# Callers: only `new Repo` at 997 (prepareNodeBootOn has one caller, openNodeVessel via line 694). selfSlotShareDecision callers: the closure, nexus-client-dial.ts (comment only at line 8; no call), and 13 test files.
# Tests: selfSlotShareDecision itself is decision-table tested (self-slot-share.test.ts, 33 cases; plus gate-widening, kahu-guard-lanes, floor-fleet-lanes, edge-shadow-ring, same-operator-refold and others, 13 files). The closure (cell derivation) is reached only through a whole boot or a hand copy (F3).
# Lift target: shared cap-stack stage in lararium-mesh. selfSlotShareDecision already imports only &#64;lararium/mesh and automerge types, so it moves as a file (name by capability: `peer-share-verdict`, port `SharePeerStanding` = {isWire, isSibling, peerClass, shadow, antigen, membership, ...}). The ShareInputs cell = one record built by the composer, handed to a pure `shareVerdictOf(inputs)`; the closure shrinks to one line. Browser fork: open-browser-vessel.ts:1961 uses the thinner `federationShareDecision(relayPeers, fedGate, ..., siblings)` with no antigen/membership/protected/shadow. If a browser vessel takes a node-like role it needs the same verdict, so one owner of the share law is the isomorphic end state.
# Laws: one owner per registry (two share laws exist today); capability not host (the move is clean: no node import); no global now (none in the decision; the yield at 1023 is ordering, not time); old shapes burn (F5 dead lanes). No key on a surface: untouched.
# Risk: ralias edits 848-900 and 1002/1251 (its tree is committed, unpushed): do not open T11 until ralias lands or the cut rebases onto it (ralias also adds a class to ProtectedDocClass in mesh and `faceGrantRing`/`reverdictLater` cells, which ShareInputs must carry). F1 (null reads open) decides cell semantics; F4 ordering must stay pinned. u1 does not touch this span (its diff has no open-node-vessel hunks).
# Red-first: (a) a table test that builds ShareInputs from stand-in cells and asserts hasWsSocket for each of: listening socket, dial-adapter peer, proven house island, proven sibling, unknown id (reads wire); control: the same table through the old closure inputs by hand copy must disagree on a planted drift. (b) "not stood" matrix: for each of antigen/shadow/protected null, a wire-peer ask withholds; control: the hand-built stood version allows the public shelf. (c) mutant: flip `houseIslands.has` polarity must go red.
# VERDICT: NEEDS-RULING. Fork: do the three null-reads-open cells (F1) become withhold-by-name in the cell (behavior tightens; safe under the order that holds today) or does the cut pin today's semantics byte for byte? Lean: tighten in the cell, red-first (a boot window answer should never rest on call order). Second small fork: burn `walkerBoard` and the walker branches with the cut. Lean: burn (old shapes burn).

!!! T13 first half ~ stage by stage (R1-R19: S1-S17)
Common: each stage lands one PR into mesh (transport-free) or tw5 (keel), browser twin burns in the same PR; the substrate stays a port implemented per host. Named ports: `GateSeat` (stand/unstand a gate on a route), `PeerSeatBook`, `CarriedLedger` (replaces `sealHome` path reads), `DocAnchorStore` (catalog pointer), `RestDoor`/`CasDoor` (u1 owns), `HearthDial`.
* S2 peer seat book (771-951). Capability: seats a proven peer. State: 7 maps keyed by peerId plus inboundUnseats; callees: peerArrivals (mesh), faceViews, membership holder. Tests: none unit; whole boot only. Target: mesh `peer-seat-book` (pure maps + clearPeer + seat(session)) behind `ArrivalSource` {onCandidate, onLeave, socketOf, closed(socket)} implemented by the ws listening adapter. Risk: F4 order; the 907 listener must precede Repo. Red: seat/unseat table incl. replacement arrival (generation identity) and a mutant dropping a map in clearInboundPeer. VERDICT CUT-READY after T6 (pins the registration order).
* S3 protected-doc holders + guard (811-861, ralias edits 848-900). Capability: withholds classed docs. VERDICT DO-NOT-CUT until ralias lands (ralias rewrites the guard wiring and adds a class and 3 cells).
* S9/S10/S12 holders (antigen 1192-1199, membership 1270-1282, carried/posture 1211-1269, edge shadow 1346-1417). Capability: refolds membership/bans/shadows. Already modules (antigen-ring 135L, nexus-carriage 591L, edge-shadow-ring 288L) taking `repo` + `sealHome`. Composer part = wiring + postureOf/contractHolds/gateNexuses (lift map's C4 pure readers, already T5). Lift: wiring into a mesh stage once `sealHome` becomes `CarriedLedger` (fs path today; 23 reads in nexus-carriage.ts). VERDICT NEEDS-RULING: shape of CarriedLedger (the browser has no seal home; reads Keyhive/IDB). Lean: port with {readNexusDoc, carriedSet, keptAdmits, keptFloorPins}, sealHome stays the node implementation. dropNoLongerHeld stays substrate (needs socket.close).
* S11 after-roll (1284-1332). Chain already extracted (after-roll-chain.ts, tested after-roll-chain.test.ts, after-roll-awaited.test.ts). Composer part is 8 lambdas. VERDICT CUT-READY (ride with the holders; no state of its own).
* S13 face gates (1420-1553). Capability: serves a gate. Cap logic = gateDeps, deviceBook, sweepSameOperator, gateNexuses, floorGates (vesselGate in vessel-gates.ts, 63L). Substrate: gateServer.stand + dispatcher.registerUpgrade + real timers. Tests: gated-node-rig (real wire), floor-fleet-lanes, same-operator-refold, flow-floor-resweep (booted). Target: `GateSeat` port; sweep logic into a mesh stage. Risk: 5 forward cells (sweepSameOperator, resweepGates, registerRelayPlanes, intentRelay, gateReadings) set from hunks far below (3272, 2440); order across 1500 lines. VERDICT NEEDS-RULING: whether the browser can ever stand a gate (needs a listening transport). Lean: keep stand/unstand as a host port, cut the sweep + deps; do it inside T12's single-owner window, not before.
* S1/S15 gate front and herm relay port: listening sockets. DO-NOT-CUT into shared stages (substrate by nature: they bind a server); keep as host adapters named by capability (`GateSeat`, `CarriageRelayPort`).
* S6/S16 rest door and cas door (1078-1089, 1595-1610). Process-global setters (setRestDoor/setCasDoor). VERDICT DO-NOT-CUT until T9/u1 lands VesselDoors (u1 touches worker-handle.ts, not this file's span, but the cut owns the same four globals).
* S7 catalog anchor (1090-1119). Fs pointer with flush-before-pointer rule (comment 1096-1103). Target: `DocAnchorStore` adapter (node fs; browser IDB) plus mesh stage for the order rule. Test: none unit; red: pointer never written before `repo.flush()` resolves (control: write-first form reds). VERDICT CUT-READY (ralias adds two `vesselPrivate.add` lines at 1154/1160: rebase).
* S14 selfSlotFedGate + hosting docs + bulb (1555-1573): pure construction; folds with T11 cells. CUT-READY with T11.
* S17 dial prep + carriage pull (1612-1695). `chooseHearthDial` (hearth-gate-pins.ts, pure), `vesselCarriagePull` (herm-carriage.ts, 153L): both already modules. Composer = option wiring. `nodeDialSocket` (21L, ws) substrate. Dial fires at 2339, outside this span. VERDICT CUT-READY for the prep; the dial itself belongs to the openDaemon read.
* S0/S5-S8 (preamble, identity, island): S0 not in the T rows; its readers (corpusRoot, bootstrapPath, hearthPin) are T16 (injected homes). Leave.
Collisions: ralias (848-900 guard; additive hunks at 727, 1002, 1154, 1160, 1251), u1 (1697 boot cells, not 709-1700 code), T6 (pins first), T12 single-owner window.

